A||||9||merlin||For you Delorean fans...||||1||
Z||000000||merlin||11-17-2001||09:27 AM||||It seems like there are a few Delorean fans on the forum and given the interest in a diecast Fiero model, I thought I'd let people know that a diecast model of the Delorean has just been released.  I used to follow some of the Delorean forums and it's interesting to note that they had the same up-hill battle to get the Delorean model created.  Actually, Sunstar is the manufacturer of the model, which is the same organization that is being petitioned to create the Fiero model.  Anyway, here's one on-line retailer (there maybe others) that's selling  the model. <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.exoticar.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.exoticar.com/</A> <BR>(Goto the search page and type 'Delorean'.)<P>In addition, you may be able to get a lower price on Ebay, but I have noticed that some people are paying more than retail on Ebay...  ...who knows why?  By the way, I don't work for Sunstar (If I did there'd be a model of the Fiero) or Exoticar.||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||11-17-2001||11:28 AM||||I got my magazine from them a few months ago and noticed that they now offer one!  It's going on my Christmas list.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Along with the new Mini, the Pantera, and a Ferrari 360.<P>I'm running out of room for all my models!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||11-26-2001||06:44 PM||||OH...<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>MY...<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>GOD!!!!<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>I just got mine today... I am in utter awe.<P>Anybody who knows me knows that I am picky as Hell about my collectibles. The only reasons I ordered this thing was because <P>A - I love DeLoreans,<P>B - it's 1/18th scale so it will match the Viper RT/10 and the Viper GTS I have on my computer desk, and <P>C - the pics looked pretty O.K., so I figured close enough is good enough in this case, since non-'Back to the Future' Delorean models are virtually nonexistant. <P><BR>As soon as I pulled the paper wrapping out of the top of the box and looked at this thing, I started drooling... I'm not exaggerating, there was a puddle soaking into the carpet while I carefully removed this thing from the box. It's THAT good.<P>This is the nicest 1/18th-scale car I have ever seen in my life. IT LOOKS LIKE REAL STAINLESS STEEL. The 'grain' of the stainless steel is even going in the proper fore-to-aft direction on all the body panels. THIS THING IS DROP-DEAD GORGEOUS!!!<P>If you like Deloreans - Hell, if you've ever seen a DeLorean - this is an absolute must-have. I have wanted a DeLorean for years, but I knew it would be a money pit. This scale reproduction has satisfied 80% of my urge to own a real one. And the best thing - IT'S ONLY THIRTY BUCKS(U.S.)!!<P>'Scuse me while I go back and drool at it some more. <P>*THANKS*, merlin, for pointing this thing out!<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
